==German==
[[Image:Foto-Exkursion Berlin 2008 05.JPG|thumb|Die deutsche Fahne vor dem Reichstag in Berlin.<br>''The German flag in front of the [[w:Reichstag|Reichstag]] in [[w:Berlin|Berlin]]''.]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|vane}} / {{m|gmh|van}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|fano}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*fanô||cloth, flag}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*pān-||fabric}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈfaːnə]|lang=de}}
* Fah·ne, plural: Fah·nen
* {{audio|De-at-Fahne.ogg|Audio (Austria)|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Fahne.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Fahnen|Fähnchen|dim2=Fähnlein}}

# a [[flag]]; a [[banner]] {{gloss|any cloth or fabric used as a symbol}}
# an [[idea]], an [[ideal]]
# the [[notice]]able [[smell]] of [[alcohol]] on one's [[breath]]

====Usage notes====
* Flags of nations or ships are more commonly called {{m|de|Flagge}}, but ''Fahne'' (being the more general term) is also possible.

